returns exactly 'Hello, world!'\"},{\"path\":\"computed:sha256:a743b65afaef26961a61def7ba50c55dbe83330eb27aa852fb7a13052fc3ceb6:/records/comparison\",\"quote\":\"\\\"residuals\\\":[\\\"raw argument-list and raw type fields are absent from the original predicate observation; strict raw-field compliance needs owner disposition\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"computed:sha256:a743b65afaef26961a61def7ba50c55dbe83330eb27aa852fb7a13052fc3ceb6:/records/constructionEdges/13\",\"quote\":\"\\\"declaredReadPath\\\":\\\"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs\\\",\\\"dependent\\\":{\\\"afterDigest\\\":\\\"sha256:c69ed6ca8f50ba55e59ff4a841856cb977a63ebdf6d2c98b81e35ba62af4ed7d\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"test-execution-plan.json\\\"}\"}]},{\"criterionRef\":\"criterion\":\"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/evidence/obligation-conservation@5\",\"disposition\":\"satisfied\",\"rationale\":\"All 14 construction edges are structurally true: declared read, unique producer, and current predecessor and dependent. Every edge also records completeReport=false, and edges 1, 6 and 10 record declaresPredecessor=false. I judged the obligations from the bodies, not from those records. Each original requirement has a realizing surface and a paired proof surface. The component and UAT obligations are realized by distinct test files that each passed separately in the retained runs (command-2, command-3), which answers the per-suite attribution pressure. The package fields, which the planned command does not exercise, have a separate retained observation (command-5: private-true, type-module, keys-exact). The document surfaces have only structural presence checks (command-6); their semantic content is judged in this assessment, not by that check. The declaresPredecessor=false records mean package.json cannot carry a JSON derivedFrom and the test comments omit package.json. That is a non-closing content observation, not a lost obligation, because both tests rely only on built-ins and ESM loading. The test_execution_result acce