ion result with no file. package.json has private:true and type:module. src/hello.mjs is a named export returning the exact literal. The test design sets a component obligation and a UAT obligation through the same export. Both tests use node:test and node:assert/strict with the exact import line and strict equality. The plan has the exact command and args, floor 2, 'fail 0' with no pass pin, and assertedReturnValue \\\"Hello, world!\\\". The additions (synchronous, no default export, exact package keys, one test per file) narrow what the source leaves open. They follow from the conformance rule that the only public behaviour is a return value, and none weakens or contradicts a source statement. One construction choice is unresolved: the test design reads full bytes where the source says 'artifact summaries' (req-pressure:03). The retention decision is justified by these bodies. The structural records alone do not establish it: every edge is verdict true, and the evidence is the content comparison above.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt\",\"quote\":\"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority.\"},{\"path\":\"original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt\",\"quote\":\"package.json must be private:true and type:module.\"},{\"path\":\"specification/project-conformance.md\",\"quote\":\"This document is the authority for design/implementation-design.md.\"},{\"path\":\"design/implementation-design.md\",\"quote\":\"Authority: specification/project-conformance.md\"},{\"path\":\"design/implementation-design.md\",\"quote\":\"declares no other field, so it adds no bin, script or other output surface.\"},{\"path\":\"package.json\",\"quote\":\"\\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\"\"},{\"path\":\"src/hello.mjs\",\"quote\":\"return \\\"Hello, world!\\\";\"},{\"path\":\"design/test-design.md\",\"quote\":\"Evidence source: package.json and src/hello.mjs\"},{\"path\":\"test/component/hello.test.mjs\",\"quote\":\"import { helloWorld } from \\